surface":"வணிகன்","parts":[{"text":"வணிகன்","lemma":"வணிகன்","gloss":"merchant"}],"gloss":"merchant"},{"surface":"ஆஅய்","parts":[{"text":"ஆஅய்","lemma":"ஆஅய்","gloss":"Ay"}],"gloss":"Ay","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அல்லன்","parts":[{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"அன்","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"he is not"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிறரும்","parts":[{"text":"பிறர்","lemma":"பிறர்","gloss":"others"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"also"}],"gloss":"others also"},{"surface":"சான்றோர்","parts":[{"text":"சான்றோர்","lemma":"சான்றோர்","gloss":"noble people"}],"gloss":"noble people"},{"surface":"சென்ற","parts":[{"text":"சென்ற","lemma":"சென்ற","gloss":"traversed"}],"gloss":"traversed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நெறி","parts":[{"text":"நெறி","lemma":"நெறி","gloss":"path"}],"gloss":"path"},{"surface":"என","parts":[{"text":"என","lemma":"என்","gloss":"saying"}],"gloss":"saying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஆங்கு","lemma":"ஆங்கு","gloss":"thus"}],"gloss":"thus"},{"surface":"பட்டன்று","parts":[{"text":"பட்டன்று","lemma":"பட்டன்று","gloss":"is established"}],"gloss":"is established","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"அவன்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"கைவண்மை","parts":[{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand"},{"text":"வண்மை","lemma":"வண்மை","gloss":"generosity"}],"gloss":"generosity of hand"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"What is done in this life will be of use in the next life, saying / Ay is not a merchant who sells virtue. / Saying, 'This is the path traversed by other noble people also,' / thus indeed is established his generosity of hand.","translation":"Ay is not a merchant trading in virtue, giving charity in this life with the expectation that it will yield rewards in the next. Rather, his generosity of hand is established simply because he knows it is the path walked by the noble ones who came before him.","modern":"இப்பிறவியில் செய்யும் தர்மம் மறுபிறவிக்குப் பயன் தரும் என்று அறத்தை விற்கும் வணிகன் அல்லன் ஆய். மற்ற சான்றோர்கள் சென்ற நல்வழி இது என்று கருதியே அவனுடைய கொடைத்தன்மை அவ்வாறு அமைந்துள்ளது.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Pāṭāṇ tiṇai and is addressed to the chieftain Āy Aṇṭiraṉ by the poet Uṟaiyūr Ēṇiccēri Muṭamōciyār. The poet praises Ay's selfless generosity, contrasting it with those who perform charitable acts out of a desire for spiritual merit or rewards in the afterlife. Ay does not treat virtue as a commercial transaction or investment for the next world. Instead, he gives freely because he believes it is the duty and the natural path established by the noble ancestors. The key phrase 'aṟavilai vaṇikaṉ' (virtue-selling merchant) beautifully captures the critique of transactional charity, highlighting Ay's pure, altruistic nature.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.1],[1.1,1.8],[1.8,2.1],[2.1,2.9],[2.9,3.1],[3.1,3.5],[3.5,3.8],[3.8,4.1],[4.1,5.3],[5.3,5.5],[5.5,5.9],[5.9,6.6],[6.6,7.2],[7.2,7.3],[7.3,7.7],[7.7,8.0],[8.0,8.6]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.6],[0.6,1.1],[1.1,1.9],[1.9,2.2],[2.2,3.3],[3.3,3.5],[3.5,4.0],[4.0,4.3],[4.3,4.7],[4.7,6.2],[6.2,6.5],[6.5,6.9],[6.9,7.7],[7.7,8.5],[8.5,8.6],[8.6,9.1],[9.1,9.5],[9.5,10.1]]}}